{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-60170","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-115436","text":"FCB — the kernellet-cost campaign: a contract, before any code (revision 2)"}]},{"id":"blk-60171","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-115437","marks":["bold"],"text":"Status:"},{"id":"spn-115438","text":" CONTRACT FOR REVIEW, revision 2 (2026-09-16), rewritten on the stage-0.1 review's findings ("},{"id":"spn-115439","marks":["code"],"text":"docs/fcb-stage01-review-2026-09-16.md"},{"id":"spn-115440","text":", \"Kernellet-cost contract review\"): the stale witness total, the wrong gate for transition-only comparators, the overstated marginal-subtraction guarantee, the "},{"id":"spn-115441","marks":["code"],"text":"CLOCK_MONOTONIC"},{"id":"spn-115442","text":" wording, and the unproven "},{"id":"spn-115443","marks":["code"],"text":"iret"},{"id":"spn-115444","text":" claim. "},{"id":"spn-115445","marks":["bold"],"text":"No code exists for this campaign and none is written until Codex has accepted this revision."},{"id":"spn-115446","text":" Nothing here is a number. This file rules nothing; it says what the campaign would measure, on what, under which two gates, which fixed costs the marginal method is "},{"id":"spn-115447","marks":["italic"],"text":"hypothesised"},{"id":"spn-115448","text":" to cancel and how that hypothesis is tested, and what would falsify it."}]},{"id":"blk-60172","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-115449","text":"0. Why a separate campaign"}]},{"id":"blk-60173","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-115450","text":"The row the scheduler-outcome benchmark calls "},{"id":"spn-115451","marks":["code"],"text":"computedriven-policy"},{"id":"spn-115452","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-115453","marks":["code"],"text":"fcb/cd/"},{"id":"spn-115454","text":") is the "},{"id":"spn-115455","marks":["bold"],"text":"cd-core policy adapter"},{"id":"spn-115456","text":": cd-core's lifecycle types, the kernellet's "},{"id":"spn-115457","marks":["code"],"text":"step"},{"id":"spn-115458","text":" "},{"id":"spn-115459","marks":["italic"],"text":"shape"},{"id":"spn-115460","text":", a benchmark-local home (RR-FAIR / CLOCK-AGE / HOT-RESIDENT), explicit parking, one thread, a standard Rust process. It does "},{"id":"spn-115461","marks":["bold"],"text":"not"},{"id":"spn-115462","text":" execute the production "},{"id":"spn-115463","marks":["code"],"text":"cd-kernellet"},{"id":"spn-115464","text":" image or its 48-byte command / 32-byte outcome ABI. It supports a claim about ComputeDriven's "},{"id":"spn-115465","marks":["italic"],"text":"scheduling policy and residency mechanism"},{"id":"spn-115466","text":"; it cannot support the stronger claim that the shipped no_std floor beats Linux, Go, BEAM or Seastar on transition price or footprint. That claim needs the real image, measured as itself. This is that campaign. "},{"id":"spn-115467","marks":["bold"],"text":"The two campaigns are never combined into one winner claim"},{"id":"spn-115468","text":" (the review's stage gate, last line; F-KC-4)."}]},{"id":"blk-60174","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-115469","text":"1. The question"}]},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-60176","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-115470","text":"What does one admitted semantic transition cost, in retired "},{"id":"spn-115471","marks":["bold"],"text":"user-domain"},{"id":"spn-115472","text":" instructions, core cycles and L1 traffic, on the production "},{"id":"spn-115473","marks":["code"],"text":"cd-kernellet"},{"id":"spn-115474","text":" ELF built from the reviewed source and driven through its own ABI, compared with a semantically equivalent "},{"id":"spn-115475","marks":["bold"],"text":"class-S transition loop"},{"id":"spn-115476","text":" in C, Go, Erlang and Rust — and what does the image and one live context cost in bytes?"}]}],"id":"blk-60175","kind":"quote"},{"id":"blk-60177","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-115477","text":"\"Semantically equivalent\" is defined by §3's shared transition-vector suite, not by the kernellet's full battery (§2): the comparators implement the transition, not the kernellet."}]},{"id":"blk-60178","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-115478","text":"2. The two gates, named honestly"}]},{"id":"blk-60179","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-115479","text":"The stage-0.1 review found revision 1 naming \"R2's 201 witnesses\" and "},{"id":"spn-115480","marks":["code"],"text":"tools/kernellet_abi.py"},{"id":"spn-115481","text":" as the battery, and asking transition-only comparators to pass the kernellet's complete external battery — which includes BOOT, table bounds, finalization, fencing, authority evidence, custody and multi-context behaviour those comparators do not implement. A shim supplying those mechanisms would test the shim. So: "},{"id":"spn-115482","marks":["bold"],"text":"two different gates."}]},{"id":"blk-60180","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-115483","text":"2.1 The subject's gate: the full kernellet census, unchanged"}]},{"id":"blk-60181","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-115484","text":"The production kernellet subject must pass "},{"id":"spn-115485","marks":["bold"],"text":"the current full census gate, unchanged, at the exact measured commit"},{"id":"spn-115486","text":": "},{"id":"spn-115487","marks":["code"],"text":"python3 tools/kernellet_census.py --check"},{"id":"spn-115488","text":", which rebuilds the images, drives each through its ABI with "},{"id":"spn-115489","marks":["code"],"text":"tools/kernellet_abi.py"},{"id":"spn-115490","text":", and diffs the receipt "},{"id":"spn-115491","marks":["code"],"text":"receipts/KERNELLET-R1.md"},{"id":"spn-115492","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-115493","marks":["code"],"text":"guards.sh"},{"id":"spn-115494","text":" runs it; a toolchain or source change fails the build by design). Its external witness battery is what "},{"id":"spn-115495","marks":["code"],"text":"receipts/KERNELLET-R1.json"},{"id":"spn-115496","text":" holds under "},{"id":"spn-115497","marks":["code"],"text":"batteries"},{"id":"spn-115498","text":", "},{"id":"spn-115499","marks":["bold"],"text":"derived, never hand-typed"},{"id":"spn-115500","text":":"}]},{"id":"blk-60182","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"python3 -c \"import json; b=json.load(open('receipts/KERNELLET-R1.json'))['batteries']; \\\nprint({k: (len(v['checks']), v['held']) for k, v in b.items()}, sum(len(v['checks']) for v in b.values()))\""},{"id":"blk-60183","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-115501","text":"At "},{"id":"spn-115502","marks":["code"],"text":"01031e6"},{"id":"spn-115503","text":" (receipt last changed at "},{"id":"spn-115504","marks":["code"],"text":"62a1c14"},{"id":"spn-115505","text":") that prints six batteries — "},{"id":"spn-115506","marks":["code"],"text":"custody-n8"},{"id":"spn-115507","text":" 46, "},{"id":"spn-115508","marks":["code"],"text":"fastmem-n8"},{"id":"spn-115509","text":" 39, "},{"id":"spn-115510","marks":["code"],"text":"prod-n1"},{"id":"spn-115511","text":" 38, "},{"id":"spn-115512","marks":["code"],"text":"prod-n128"},{"id":"spn-115513","text":" 39, "},{"id":"spn-115514","marks":["code"],"text":"prod-n8"},{"id":"spn-115515","text":" 39, "},{"id":"spn-115516","marks":["code"],"text":"ring-n8"},{"id":"spn-115517","text":" 39 — "},{"id":"spn-115518","marks":["bold"],"text":"240 witness objects, 240 held"},{"id":"spn-115519","text":", the total the review re-derived. The campaign's receipt re-derives it the same way at its own commit and quotes nothing else. (Revision 1's \"201\" was R1's count at an earlier commit, copied from memory: exactly the drift "},{"id":"spn-115520","marks":["code"],"text":"tools/counts_gate.py"},{"id":"spn-115521","text":" exists to refuse.)"}]},{"id":"blk-60184","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-115522","text":"2.2 Every measured row's gate: the class-S transition-vector suite (new; part of this campaign)"}]},{"id":"blk-60185","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-115523","text":"One shared suite, limited to the semantics actually priced, that "},{"id":"spn-115524","marks":["bold"],"text":"every row — the kernellet included — must pass"},{"id":"spn-115525","text":" before its timing run is admitted:"}]},{"id":"blk-60186","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-60188","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-115526","text":"possession dispatch: ATTACH on Vacant → Attached; DETACH on Attached → Vacant; the inadmissible"}]}],"id":"blk-60187","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-60189","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-115527","text":"op → "},{"id":"spn-115528","marks":["code"],"text":"BAD_POSSESSION"},{"id":"spn-115529","text":" (2, 6) with the lineage unchanged;"}]},{"id":"blk-60190","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-60192","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-115530","text":"generation and transition evolution: DETACH increments "},{"id":"spn-115531","marks":["code"],"text":"generation"},{"id":"spn-115532","text":"; both increment"}]}],"id":"blk-60191","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-60193","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-115533","marks":["code"],"text":"transitions"},{"id":"spn-115534","text":"; a DETACH whose "},{"id":"spn-115535","marks":["code"],"text":"gen_at_attach ≠ generation"},{"id":"spn-115536","text":" is "},{"id":"spn-115537","marks":["code"],"text":"REFUSED WrongGeneration"},{"id":"spn-115538","text":" (1, 4);"}]},{"id":"blk-60194","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-60196","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-115539","text":"copy-in / copy-out: the step works on a copy and writes back only on success — **the original"}]}],"id":"blk-60195","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-60197","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-115540","text":"survives every refusal byte-for-byte**;"}]},{"id":"blk-60198","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-60200","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-115541","text":"the common digest ("},{"id":"spn-115542","marks":["code"],"text":"docs/fcb-model.md"},{"id":"spn-115543","text":" §4) over a fixed vector of ops from a fixed seed, so"}]}],"id":"blk-60199","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-60201","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-115544","text":"a row that skipped a check or a fold differs in one number."}]},{"id":"blk-60202","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-115545","text":"The suite is a fixed vector file ("},{"id":"spn-115546","marks":["code"],"text":"fcb/kc/vectors.json"},{"id":"spn-115547","text":": op sequences, expected outcomes, expected "},{"id":"spn-115548","marks":["code"],"text":"generation"},{"id":"spn-115549","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-115550","marks":["code"],"text":"transitions"},{"id":"spn-115551","text":", expected digests) plus one tiny driver per row that feeds the vector to that row's transition loop and prints the digest and the final state. "},{"id":"spn-115552","marks":["bold"],"text":"Its non-vacuity: a `skip-copy-out` mutant"},{"id":"spn-115553","text":" (the step writes back on refusal too) and a "},{"id":"spn-115554","marks":["code"],"text":"skip-generation-check"},{"id":"spn-115555","text":" mutant, each in one row, must be caught by the suite before the first timing run. The kernellet passes the suite through its ABI (BEGIN, ATTACH/DETACH per vector op, the outcome frames); it passes §2.1 besides. A comparator passes only §2.2, and that is all it claims."}]},{"id":"blk-60203","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-115556","text":"3. The subject and the comparators, exactly"}]},{"id":"blk-60204","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-60206","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-115557","marks":["bold"],"text":"Subject:"},{"id":"spn-115558","text":" "},{"id":"spn-115559","marks":["code"],"text":"cd-kernellet"},{"id":"spn-115560","text":" built by "},{"id":"spn-115561","marks":["code"],"text":"tools/kernellet_abi.py K.build(features, n)"},{"id":"spn-115562","text":" from the commit"}]}],"id":"blk-60205","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-60207","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-115563","text":"named in the receipt, in the two profiles the census names — "},{"id":"spn-115564","marks":["code"],"text":"prod"},{"id":"spn-115565","text":" (no features) and "},{"id":"spn-115566","marks":["code"],"text":"fastmem"},{"id":"spn-115567","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-115568","marks":["code"],"text":"rep movsb"},{"id":"spn-115569","text":" copies) — at "},{"id":"spn-115570","marks":["code"],"text":"n ∈ {1, 8, 32, 128}"},{"id":"spn-115571","text":" contexts (the census's own "},{"id":"spn-115572","marks":["code"],"text":"n"},{"id":"spn-115573","text":" set is the source of truth; the receipt lists what it used). Layout: the kernellet's own table, "},{"id":"spn-115574","marks":["bold"],"text":"312 B per context"},{"id":"spn-115575","text":" (the census's slope of "},{"id":"spn-115576","marks":["code"],"text":".data + .bss"},{"id":"spn-115577","text":" over "},{"id":"spn-115578","marks":["code"],"text":"n"},{"id":"spn-115579","text":"), one shared stack."}]},{"id":"blk-60208","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-60210","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-115580","marks":["bold"],"text":"Drive:"},{"id":"spn-115581","text":" the image's own ABI. "},{"id":"spn-115582","marks":["code"],"text":"BOOT"},{"id":"spn-115583","text":", "},{"id":"spn-115584","marks":["code"],"text":"BEGIN"},{"id":"spn-115585","text":" per context, then "},{"id":"spn-115586","marks":["bold"],"text":"one `BENCH n iters` command"}]}],"id":"blk-60209","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-60211","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-115587","text":"that performs "},{"id":"spn-115588","marks":["code"],"text":"2 · n · iters"},{"id":"spn-115589","text":" attach/detach transitions "},{"id":"spn-115590","marks":["italic"],"text":"inside the image"},{"id":"spn-115591","text":", then "},{"id":"spn-115592","marks":["code"],"text":"HIST"},{"id":"spn-115593","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-115594","marks":["code"],"text":"STACKHW"},{"id":"spn-115595","text":" reads ("},{"id":"spn-115596","marks":["code"],"text":"tools/kernellet_bench.py stream()"},{"id":"spn-115597","text":"). The host writes a handful of commands per run; "},{"id":"spn-115598","marks":["bold"],"text":"no per-transition IPC exists on this path"},{"id":"spn-115599","text":", so host pipe cost is not in the number. This is the census path that already exists; the campaign adds comparators to it, not a new driver."}]},{"id":"blk-60212","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-60214","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-115600","marks":["bold"],"text":"NOT the subject:"},{"id":"spn-115601","text":" a pipe-per-transition \"end-to-end\" row. The review forbids calling host IPC"}]}],"id":"blk-60213","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-60215","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-115602","text":"overhead the floor, and this contract does not build one."}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-60217","spans":[{"id":"spn-115603","text":"row"}]},{"id":"blk-60218","spans":[{"id":"spn-115604","text":"code"}]},{"id":"blk-60219","spans":[{"id":"spn-115605","text":"record layout"}]},{"id":"blk-60220","spans":[{"id":"spn-115606","text":"what it is"}]}],"id":"blk-60216","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-60221","spans":[{"id":"spn-115607","marks":["code"],"text":"cd-kernellet prod"}]},{"id":"blk-60222","spans":[{"id":"spn-115608","text":"the ELF"}]},{"id":"blk-60223","spans":[{"id":"spn-115609","text":"312 B/context in the image's table"}]},{"id":"blk-60224","spans":[{"id":"spn-115610","text":"the subject"}]}],[{"id":"blk-60225","spans":[{"id":"spn-115611","marks":["code"],"text":"cd-kernellet fastmem"}]},{"id":"blk-60226","spans":[{"id":"spn-115612","text":"the ELF, "},{"id":"spn-115613","marks":["code"],"text":"rep movsb"},{"id":"spn-115614","text":" copies"}]},{"id":"blk-60227","spans":[{"id":"spn-115615","text":"312 B/context"}]},{"id":"blk-60228","spans":[{"id":"spn-115616","text":"the subject's second profile"}]}],[{"id":"blk-60229","spans":[{"id":"spn-115617","marks":["code"],"text":"c-class-S"}]},{"id":"blk-60230","spans":[{"id":"spn-115618","marks":["code"],"text":"sflr/c/lineage.h"},{"id":"spn-115619","text":" + "},{"id":"spn-115620","marks":["code"],"text":"step_inc.h"},{"id":"spn-115621","text":" "},{"id":"spn-115622","marks":["code"],"text":"VARIANT 1"},{"id":"spn-115623","text":" in a "},{"id":"spn-115624","marks":["code"],"text":"n × iters"},{"id":"spn-115625","text":" loop"}]},{"id":"blk-60231","spans":[{"id":"spn-115626","text":"312 B "},{"id":"spn-115627","marks":["code"],"text":"lineage_t"},{"id":"spn-115628","text":", an array of "},{"id":"spn-115629","marks":["code"],"text":"n"}]},{"id":"blk-60232","spans":[{"id":"spn-115630","text":"the R2 witness battery's C SUT shape"}]}],[{"id":"blk-60233","spans":[{"id":"spn-115631","marks":["code"],"text":"go-class-S"}]},{"id":"blk-60234","spans":[{"id":"spn-115632","marks":["code"],"text":"sflr/go/sut.go"},{"id":"spn-115633","text":" "},{"id":"spn-115634","marks":["code"],"text":"step"},{"id":"spn-115635","text":" in the same loop"}]},{"id":"blk-60235","spans":[{"id":"spn-115636","text":"312 B "},{"id":"spn-115637","marks":["code"],"text":"Lineage"},{"id":"spn-115638","text":", a slice of "},{"id":"spn-115639","marks":["code"],"text":"n"}]},{"id":"blk-60236","spans":[{"id":"spn-115640","text":"the R2 Go SUT shape"}]}],[{"id":"blk-60237","spans":[{"id":"spn-115641","marks":["code"],"text":"erl-class-S"}]},{"id":"blk-60238","spans":[{"id":"spn-115642","marks":["code"],"text":"sflr/erl/sut.erl"},{"id":"spn-115643","text":" "},{"id":"spn-115644","marks":["code"],"text":"step"},{"id":"spn-115645","text":" in the same loop"}]},{"id":"blk-60239","spans":[{"id":"spn-115646","text":"Erlang terms (no byte layout; reported as such)"}]},{"id":"blk-60240","spans":[{"id":"spn-115647","text":"the R2 Erlang SUT shape"}]}],[{"id":"blk-60241","spans":[{"id":"spn-115648","marks":["code"],"text":"rust-cd-core"}]},{"id":"blk-60242","spans":[{"id":"spn-115649","marks":["code"],"text":"cd-core"},{"id":"spn-115650","text":" "},{"id":"spn-115651","marks":["code"],"text":"VacantLocus::attach"},{"id":"spn-115652","text":" / "},{"id":"spn-115653","marks":["code"],"text":"LocusAttachment::detach"},{"id":"spn-115654","text":" in the same loop"}]},{"id":"blk-60243","spans":[{"id":"spn-115655","text":"144 B "},{"id":"spn-115656","marks":["code"],"text":"Lineage"},{"id":"spn-115657","text":" (cd-core's types, no authority ring), a "},{"id":"spn-115658","marks":["code"],"text":"Vec"},{"id":"spn-115659","text":" of "},{"id":"spn-115660","marks":["code"],"text":"n"}]},{"id":"blk-60244","spans":[{"id":"spn-115661","text":"the floor's own types without the ring"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-60245","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-115662","text":"Every comparator: the same loop shape as the image's "},{"id":"spn-115663","marks":["code"],"text":"BENCH"},{"id":"spn-115664","text":" op ("},{"id":"spn-115665","marks":["code"],"text":"iters"},{"id":"spn-115666","text":" iterations, each one ATTACH then one DETACH on every context in index order), the class-S step, the digest folded so partial work is visible, the result printed once at the end. No scheduler, no mailbox, no pipe, no clock read per transition: this campaign prices the "},{"id":"spn-115667","marks":["italic"],"text":"transition"},{"id":"spn-115668","text":"; the scheduler-outcome campaign prices the "},{"id":"spn-115669","marks":["italic"],"text":"scheduling"},{"id":"spn-115670","text":". Toolchains and flags are pinned and printed (rustc 1.75, "},{"id":"spn-115671","marks":["code"],"text":"opt-level = \"s\""},{"id":"spn-115672","text":" for the image and the Rust comparator; "},{"id":"spn-115673","marks":["code"],"text":"gcc -O2"},{"id":"spn-115674","text":"; the Go and OTP versions)."}]},{"id":"blk-60246","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-115675","text":"4. The instrument, and what the marginal method is hypothesised to cancel"}]},{"id":"blk-60247","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-115676","text":"Runs per (row, n): "},{"id":"spn-115677","marks":["code"],"text":"iters = K"},{"id":"spn-115678","text":", "},{"id":"spn-115679","marks":["code"],"text":"2K"},{"id":"spn-115680","text":" "},{"id":"spn-115681","marks":["bold"],"text":"and `4K`"},{"id":"spn-115682","text":", "},{"id":"spn-115683","marks":["code"],"text":"K"},{"id":"spn-115684","text":" sized so a run is ≥ 200,000 transitions. Per-transition figures are "},{"id":"spn-115685","marks":["code"],"text":"(counter(2K) − counter(K)) / (transitions(2K) − transitions(K))"},{"id":"spn-115686","text":", median of 5 repeats — "},{"id":"spn-115687","marks":["code"],"text":"tools/kernellet_bench.py"},{"id":"spn-115688","text":"'s method — "},{"id":"spn-115689","marks":["bold"],"text":"admitted only if the `K`/`2K`/`4K` points are linear"},{"id":"spn-115690","text":" (§4.2)."}]},{"id":"blk-60248","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-115691","text":"4.1 The cancellation hypothesis (tested, not assumed)"}]},{"id":"blk-60249","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-115692","text":"K/2K subtraction removes costs that are "},{"id":"spn-115693","marks":["bold"],"text":"fixed per process at constant `n`"},{"id":"spn-115694","text":". Which costs are fixed is a "},{"id":"spn-115695","marks":["bold"],"text":"hypothesis about each row"},{"id":"spn-115696","text":", listed here so the linearity check can refute it: process exec and image load; "},{"id":"spn-115697","marks":["code"],"text":"BOOT"},{"id":"spn-115698","text":" and the "},{"id":"spn-115699","marks":["code"],"text":"n"},{"id":"spn-115700","text":" "},{"id":"spn-115701","marks":["code"],"text":"BEGIN"},{"id":"spn-115702","text":"s; the "},{"id":"spn-115703","marks":["code"],"text":"HIST"},{"id":"spn-115704","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-115705","marks":["code"],"text":"STACKHW"},{"id":"spn-115706","text":" reads; the harness's own instructions before the counters enable; first-touch page faults of the table and stack; and, for the language rows, runtime boot (Go, BEAM), JIT or loader work, and GC or runtime-service work "},{"id":"spn-115707","marks":["italic"],"text":"that does not grow with the transition count"},{"id":"spn-115708","text":". Revision 1 stated these as guaranteed by the arithmetic; the arithmetic guarantees nothing about them — a cost that grows with "},{"id":"spn-115709","marks":["code"],"text":"iters"},{"id":"spn-115710","text":" (a GC whose work is proportional to allocation, a first-touch that recurs, a service thread that wakes per unit of work) survives the subtraction and belongs in the number, and the only way to know which is to measure a third point."}]},{"id":"blk-60250","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-115711","text":"4.2 The K/2K/4K linearity check (F-KC-3, executable)"}]},{"id":"blk-60251","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-115712","text":"For each (row, n, counter), the slope from "},{"id":"spn-115713","marks":["code"],"text":"K"},{"id":"spn-115714","text":"→"},{"id":"spn-115715","marks":["code"],"text":"2K"},{"id":"spn-115716","text":" and from "},{"id":"spn-115717","marks":["code"],"text":"2K"},{"id":"spn-115718","text":"→"},{"id":"spn-115719","marks":["code"],"text":"4K"},{"id":"spn-115720","text":" must agree within the repeat dispersion (the larger of the two RSDs, floor 2 %). If they do not, the row is "},{"id":"spn-115721","marks":["bold"],"text":"NONLINEAR"},{"id":"spn-115722","text":" for that counter: the receipt prints the three raw points and their repeat spread and "},{"id":"spn-115723","marks":["bold"],"text":"withholds the marginal"},{"id":"spn-115724","text":"; no per-transition figure is quoted for it. A row may be linear on cycles and nonlinear on L1 misses; each counter is judged alone."}]},{"id":"blk-60252","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-115725","text":"4.3 What remains in a linear row's number, deliberately"}]},{"id":"blk-60253","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-115726","text":"The transition itself; the image's command-loop dispatch to it ("},{"id":"spn-115727","marks":["code"],"text":"step(ctx, input) → outcome"},{"id":"spn-115728","text":" through the ABI "},{"id":"spn-115729","marks":["italic"],"text":"shape"},{"id":"spn-115730","text":", not the ABI's I/O); the "},{"id":"spn-115731","marks":["code"],"text":"rdtsc"},{"id":"spn-115732","text":" pair when the image's bench op stamps its histogram (its own column, never subtracted); the language row's per-iteration loop and digest fold (the same fold on every row); cache effects at "},{"id":"spn-115733","marks":["code"],"text":"n"},{"id":"spn-115734","text":" (the L1D cliff at n = 128 is a finding, not noise); and any runtime work that "},{"id":"spn-115735","marks":["italic"],"text":"is"},{"id":"spn-115736","text":" proportional to transitions, which §4.2 has then shown to be linear and which is a real cost of that row."}]},{"id":"blk-60254","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-115737","text":"4.4 Counters and their domain"}]},{"id":"blk-60255","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-115738","marks":["bold"],"text":"User-domain"},{"id":"spn-115739","text":" hardware "},{"id":"spn-115740","marks":["code"],"text":"instructions"},{"id":"spn-115741","text":", "},{"id":"spn-115742","marks":["code"],"text":"cycles"},{"id":"spn-115743","text":", "},{"id":"spn-115744","marks":["code"],"text":"branches"},{"id":"spn-115745","text":", "},{"id":"spn-115746","marks":["code"],"text":"l1d_access"},{"id":"spn-115747","text":", "},{"id":"spn-115748","marks":["code"],"text":"l1d_miss"},{"id":"spn-115749","text":", "},{"id":"spn-115750","marks":["code"],"text":"l1i_miss"},{"id":"spn-115751","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-115752","marks":["code"],"text":"perf_event_paranoid = 2"},{"id":"spn-115753","text":" forces "},{"id":"spn-115754","marks":["code"],"text":"exclude_kernel"},{"id":"spn-115755","text":"). The cross-language column is therefore named "},{"id":"spn-115756","marks":["bold"],"text":"user-domain transition-loop cost"},{"id":"spn-115757","text":": the subject's path has no kernel work, so the domain is complete for it; a language row's kernel-side runtime work (Go's sysmon wakeups, BEAM's schedulers' syscalls) is outside the domain and is printed beside as "},{"id":"spn-115758","marks":["code"],"text":"sys"},{"id":"spn-115759","text":" time and "},{"id":"spn-115760","marks":["code"],"text":"rusage"},{"id":"spn-115761","text":" switches, never subtracted and never called zero. Counters are enabled and disabled by the harness around the "},{"id":"spn-115762","marks":["code"],"text":"BENCH"},{"id":"spn-115763","text":" command (the stage-0.2 window mechanism), so exec, boot and exit are outside the counted interval as well as cancelled. Multiplexed readings are dropped (R2's rule)."}]},{"id":"blk-60256","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-115764","marks":["bold"],"text":"Noise term, stated as what is known and what is not:"},{"id":"spn-115765","text":" R1 observed that the instruction column drifts with interrupt rate and load, and reported "},{"id":"spn-115766","marks":["code"],"text":"branches"},{"id":"spn-115767","text":" beside it because branches retired is the deterministic counter on this ISA. Revision 1 asserted the mechanism — that a hardware interrupt's "},{"id":"spn-115768","marks":["code"],"text":"iret"},{"id":"spn-115769","text":" retires as a user instruction. "},{"id":"spn-115770","marks":["bold"],"text":"This contract does not assert it."},{"id":"spn-115771","text":" The campaign either cites direct evidence for the mechanism (vendor documentation for this CPU model, named in the receipt) or demonstrates it with a control (a fixed user loop under two interrupt rates, the instruction delta against the branch delta), or reports the drift as observed and unexplained. What is asserted: the campaign runs only under "},{"id":"spn-115772","marks":["code"],"text":"docs/battery-host-profile.md"},{"id":"spn-115773","text":", and "},{"id":"spn-115774","marks":["code"],"text":"branches"},{"id":"spn-115775","text":" is printed beside "},{"id":"spn-115776","marks":["code"],"text":"instructions"},{"id":"spn-115777","text":" on every row."}]},{"id":"blk-60257","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-115778","text":"4.5 Footprint"}]},{"id":"blk-60258","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-115779","marks":["code"],"text":".text + .rodata"},{"id":"spn-115780","text":" of the image by "},{"id":"spn-115781","marks":["code"],"text":"readelf"},{"id":"spn-115782","text":" (the census); per-context bytes as the slope of "},{"id":"spn-115783","marks":["code"],"text":".data + .bss"},{"id":"spn-115784","text":" over "},{"id":"spn-115785","marks":["code"],"text":"n"},{"id":"spn-115786","text":" (312 B/context in R1); for the language rows, the process's own "},{"id":"spn-115787","marks":["code"],"text":"VmHWM"},{"id":"spn-115788","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-115789","marks":["code"],"text":"/proc/self/status"},{"id":"spn-115790","text":", read by the row at exit — "},{"id":"spn-115791","marks":["code"],"text":"rusage"},{"id":"spn-115792","text":" maxrss is floored at the spawner's address space at exec, a stage-0.1 finding) and its Theil–Sen slope over "},{"id":"spn-115793","marks":["code"],"text":"n ∈ {8, 32, 128}"},{"id":"spn-115794","text":" × 3 repeats with min/max — the two footprint numbers are of different kinds (static image vs live process) and are printed in different columns, never compared as one."}]},{"id":"blk-60259","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-115795","text":"4.6 The clock"}]},{"id":"blk-60260","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-115796","marks":["code"],"text":"CLOCK_MONOTONIC"},{"id":"spn-115797","text":" is the shared monotonic clock domain for every timestamp the campaign records (counter edges, run boundaries). It is not changed discontinuously by wall-clock setting; its rate may be adjusted, which every process sees alike. Nothing here needs more than a shared domain."}]},{"id":"blk-60261","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-115798","text":"5. What this campaign cannot say"}]},{"id":"blk-60262","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-60264","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-115799","text":"Nothing about scheduling, fairness, tails, residency or refusal under contention — that is the"}]}],"id":"blk-60263","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-60265","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-115800","text":"other campaign, on the other row."}]},{"id":"blk-60266","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-60268","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-115801","text":"Nothing about the ABI's I/O cost per transition — the path measured does not pay it."}]}],"id":"blk-60267","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-60270","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-115802","text":"Nothing about a language row's "},{"id":"spn-115803","marks":["italic"],"text":"runtime"},{"id":"spn-115804","text":" — only its transition loop, and only in the user domain."}]}],"id":"blk-60269","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-60272","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-115805","text":"No cross-ISA claim (x86-64, rustc 1.75, "},{"id":"spn-115806","marks":["code"],"text":"opt-level = \"s\""},{"id":"spn-115807","text":" only)."}]}],"id":"blk-60271","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-60274","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-115808","text":"Nothing before it runs under the dedicated-host profile with the sentinel gates, and nothing"}]}],"id":"blk-60273","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-60275","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-115809","text":"from a development smoke."}]},{"id":"blk-60276","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-60278","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-115810","text":"Nothing from a row the linearity check marked NONLINEAR, beyond its raw points."}]}],"id":"blk-60277","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-60279","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-115811","text":"6. Falsifiers"}]},{"id":"blk-60280","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-60282","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-115812","marks":["bold"],"text":"F-KC-1"},{"id":"spn-115813","text":" — a comparator that skips a check the class-S suite names (copy-out, generation match,"}]}],"id":"blk-60281","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-60283","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-115814","text":"the original surviving a refusal, the fold) is not equivalent; the §2.2 suite must reject it, and the "},{"id":"spn-115815","marks":["code"],"text":"skip-copy-out"},{"id":"spn-115816","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-115817","marks":["code"],"text":"skip-generation-check"},{"id":"spn-115818","text":" mutants must be caught before the first timing run."}]},{"id":"blk-60284","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-60286","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-115819","marks":["bold"],"text":"F-KC-2"},{"id":"spn-115820","text":" — an image whose feature set or toolchain differs from the reviewed floor's is a"}]}],"id":"blk-60285","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-60287","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-115821","text":"different subject; the receipt names both and the census gate (§2.1) must pass at the same commit with its witness total re-derived there."}]},{"id":"blk-60288","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-60290","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-115822","marks":["bold"],"text":"F-KC-3"},{"id":"spn-115823","text":" — a marginal quoted from a row whose "},{"id":"spn-115824","marks":["code"],"text":"K"},{"id":"spn-115825","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-115826","marks":["code"],"text":"2K"},{"id":"spn-115827","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-115828","marks":["code"],"text":"4K"},{"id":"spn-115829","text":" slopes disagree beyond the repeat"}]}],"id":"blk-60289","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-60291","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-115830","text":"dispersion (§4.2)."}]},{"id":"blk-60292","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-60294","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-115831","marks":["bold"],"text":"F-KC-4"},{"id":"spn-115832","text":" — any sentence that carries this campaign's number into the scheduler-outcome"}]}],"id":"blk-60293","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-60295","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-115833","text":"frontier, or the reverse."}]},{"id":"blk-60296","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-60298","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-115834","marks":["bold"],"text":"F-KC-5"},{"id":"spn-115835","text":" — a cross-language cost column not labelled user-domain, or a kernel-side runtime"}]}],"id":"blk-60297","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-60299","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-115836","text":"cost subtracted or read as zero (§4.4)."}]},{"id":"blk-60300","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-60302","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-115837","marks":["bold"],"text":"F-KC-6"},{"id":"spn-115838","text":" — the interrupt-return mechanism asserted without the evidence or the control §4.4"}]}],"id":"blk-60301","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-60303","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-115839","text":"names."}]},{"id":"blk-60304","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-115840","text":"7. Stop"}]},{"id":"blk-60305","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-115841","text":"This is the revised contract. "},{"id":"spn-115842","marks":["bold"],"text":"Codex reviews it; then, if accepted, code is written to it — the §2.2 suite and its mutants first, the comparators second, the campaign runner last; then the campaign runs only under `docs/battery-host-profile.md` after its own authorization."},{"id":"spn-115843","text":" Not before."}]}],"edges":[],"id":"bagaaierahszdpwuyhzng2obiin7fhgbjmsbrh7xragjhg3w4rz67yj4nrxea","vocabulary":"ampersand.docs.fs.v1"}